From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: hy320: the lamp's PWM words reach no pad

The six [PWMSetting] words name channel 5. The display firmware's
channel 5 is the d_pwm5 pin function, and the stock 5.4 kernel's pin
table has it on one pad only, PG7 (mux 7) - on this board the Bluetooth
UART1 RX (stock uart1@0 PG6..PG9). On the unit (01.11.2026) the
firmware has had the words and level 100 since 5 s: PG7 stays uart1, no
pad carries a d_pwm function, and the PWM block at 0x02000c00 reads 0
throughout. Stock's backlight path (libtvpq ThalDevice::deviceSetBackLight
-> ge2d_dev ARM PWM 3) reaches no pad either: pwm3 is disabled in the
stock tree and PB5 is driven as the GPIO panel_bl_en. The words stay,
because stock's PanelControl sends them too; the comments no longer
call them the lamp's dimmer.

